WHAT IT IS
----------

- gstqvconv plugin is a video processing plugin to transform raw yuv data from one
  format/resolution to another.

FEATURES:
- Color converision: for now, only support UYVY->NV12.
- Scaling: support resolution up/down scaling.
- Flipping: support horizontal and vertical flipping.
- More features(buffer blending, buffer sharing with H/W encoder) might get added later on.

Note:
-By default qvconv will not do resolution scaling and flip, if you want to scale the image, please specify the input and output caps and property.
-If the input and output caps are equal, qvconv will enable passthrough mode, which means the input buffer will be pushed to down stream directly.

HOW TO USE/TEST IT
-------------

- videotestsrc->c2d->waylandsink
  1. down scaling:
  gst-launch-1.0 videotestsrc ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=640,height=480 ! waylandsink
  1. converision + horizontal fliping:
  gst-launch-1.0 videotestsrc ! video/x-raw, format=UYVY, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv method=1 ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1280,height=720 ! waylandsink
  2. conversion + up scaling:
  gst-launch-1.0 videotestsrc ! video/x-raw, format=UYVY, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1920,height=1080 ! waylandsink

- qcarcamsrc->c2d->waylandsink
  1. down scaling:
  gst-launch-1.0 qcarcamsrc ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=640,height=480 ! waylandsink
  2. converision + vertical fliping:
  gst-launch-1.0 qcarcamsrc ! video/x-raw, format=UYVY, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv method=2 ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1280,height=720 ! waylandsink
  3. conversion + up scaling:
  gst-launch-1.0 qcarcamsrc ! video/x-raw, format=UYVY, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1920,height=1080 ! waylandsink

- qcarcamsrc->c2d->omxh264enc->filesrc
  1. converision:
  gst-launch-1.0 qcarcamsrc ! video/x-raw, format=UYVY, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1280,height=720 ! omxh264enc ! \
  filesink location  =/data/test.264
  2. conversion + up scaling:
  gst-launch-1.0 qcarcamsrc ! video/x-raw, format=UYVY, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1920,height=1080 ! omxh264enc ! \
  filesink location  =/data/test.264
  3. conversion + down scaling:
  gst-launch-1.0 qcarcamsrc ! video/x-raw, format=UYVY, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=640,height=480 ! omxh264enc ! \
  filesink location  =/data/test.264

- qcarcamsrc->filesrc->decodebin->qvconv->waylandsink
  gst-launch-1.0 filesrc location=”test.mp4” ! decodebin ! qvconv method=1 ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=640, height=480 ! waylandsink

- multi-instance:
  1. multi-process (preview + encode):
  gst-launch-1.0 videotestsrc ! video/x-raw, format=UYVY, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1280,height=720 ! waylandsink & \
  gst-launch-1.0 qcarcamsrc ! video/x-raw, format=UYVY, width=1280,height=720 ! qvconv ! video/x-raw, format=NV12, width=1920,height=1080 ! omxh264enc ! \
  filesink location=/data/test.264

  2. multi-thread (preview + dump + encode)
  gst-launch-1.0 -v tee name=t \
  qcarcamsrc ! video/x-raw,format=UYVY,width=1280,height=720 ! t. \
  t.src_0 ! queue ! qvconv ! video/x-raw,format=NV12,width=1280,height=720 ! waylandsink \
  t.src_1 ! queue ! qvconv ! video/x-raw,format=NV12,width=1280,height=720 ! filesink location=test.yuv \
  t.src_2 ! queue ! qvconv ! video/x-raw,format=NV12,width=1280,height=720 ! omxh264enc ! filesink location=test.264
